{
  "formTitle": "DV-160 Request to Keep Minor's Information Confidential",
  "_comment": "DV-160 is the filer's request, filed with DV-100 when the case includes sensitive information about a minor (DV-100 page 1 points to DV-160-INFO). Every field but the case number and the form's buttons is the filer's. What the packet already knows carries the packet's names: the court and the two parties (DV-100 items 1 and 2), the filer's mailing address, phone, fax, email and lawyer (DV-100 item 1), and the minors, which are the children DV-100 asks under DV-105's block name - the same four rows DV-140 item 3 fills. The person making the request (item 2a) is the filer. Everything new is dv160_. The 5c(2) table is mapped by geometry, not XFA order: the left column is the location, the right the information, and the rows run (a)=[0], (b)=[3], (c)=[2], (d)=[1].",
